From a6807d1d2454d0b62dc1818d57c1f69012360355 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Mabe <alex@melonamin.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 11:23:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(image): add explicit ext4 UUID and descriptor APIs

Format caller-owned files without reopening their paths and rewrite clone UUIDs without invalidating metadata checksums. Keep legacy formatter images growable, but require explicit checksum seeds for safe UUID rewrites.

Bump the ext4 materializer ABI because newly formatted images enable INCOMPAT_CSUM_SEED.

On Unix, identify disk-image attachments by device and inode without canonicalizing their caller
paths, so inherited `/proc/self/fd/<n>` and `/dev/fd/<n>` attachments remain valid.

